From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:50:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0790/3799] soh: rename func_80002384 -> Assert_Fail

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: prints the failed expression with its file and line, then spins forever -- the assert-failure handler. Not named __assert: that would clash with libc in a PC port (cf. Math_FMod).
Defined in soh/src/boot/is_debug.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/include/functions.h | 2 +-
 soh/src/boot/is_debug.c | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/include/functions.h b/soh/include/functions.h
index 7b6d23b3f..6904e8d39 100644
--- a/soh/include/functions.h
+++ b/soh/include/functions.h
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ void osSyncPrintfUnused(const char* fmt, ...);
 //void osSyncPrintf(const char* fmt, ...);
 void rmonPrintf(const char* fmt, ...);
 void* is_proutSyncPrintf(void* arg, const char* str, u32 count);
-void func_80002384(const char* exp, const char* file, u32 line);
+void Assert_Fail(const char* exp, const char* file, u32 line);  // was func_80002384 [LLM:HIGH]
 OSPiHandle* osDriveRomInit(void);
 void StackCheck_Init(StackEntry* entry, void* stackTop, void* stackBottom, u32 initValue, s32 minSpace,
                      const char* name);
diff --git a/soh/src/boot/is_debug.c b/soh/src/boot/is_debug.c
index 2bc5e2d21..e84cd2be4 100644
--- a/soh/src/boot/is_debug.c
+++ b/soh/src/boot/is_debug.c
@@ -82,7 +82,8 @@ void* is_proutSyncPrintf(void* arg, const char* str, u32 count) {
     return 1;
 }
 
-void func_80002384(const char* exp, const char* file, u32 line) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80002384: prints the failed expression with its file and line, then spins forever -- the assert-failure handler. Not named __assert: that would clash with libc in a PC port (cf. Math_FMod).
+void Assert_Fail(const char* exp, const char* file, u32 line) {
     osSyncPrintf("File:%s Line:%d  %s \n", file, line, exp);
     while (true) {
         ;
